WEBVTT

00:07.841 --> 00:09.425
Swear to me that
everything you said

00:09.426 --> 00:11.011
about the Fireflies is true.

00:16.057 --> 00:17.350
I swear.

00:32.615 --> 00:33.616
Okay.

00:39.330 --> 00:40.832
[sighs]

00:42.333 --> 00:43.334
[sniffles]

01:03.980 --> 01:05.982
[birds chirping]

01:10.653 --> 01:12.655
[♪ gentle music playing]

01:19.037 --> 01:20.872
[giraffes softly grunting]

01:32.967 --> 01:34.969
[♪ gentle music continues]

01:46.231 --> 01:48.149
[Manny]
Why would he do this?

01:48.775 --> 01:51.026
I heard rumors.

01:51.027 --> 01:53.403
It was some kid he took
that was supposedly--

01:53.404 --> 01:56.281
- That wasn't true.
- Supposedly what?

01:56.282 --> 01:59.201
Something not true.

01:59.202 --> 02:00.869
Because it isn't possible.

02:00.870 --> 02:03.789
[Nora]
No. Probably not.

02:03.790 --> 02:05.958
And even if it were,
it doesn't fucking
matter anyway.

02:05.959 --> 02:07.418
- Not without--
- Enough.

02:11.089 --> 02:12.924
You want to worry about
something, worry about us.

02:15.552 --> 02:19.221
So, what do we do?
Do we look for other Fireflies?

02:19.222 --> 02:20.807
Where?

02:22.600 --> 02:24.727
This place was the Fireflies.

02:27.063 --> 02:29.940
Ed has a brother
who runs an outfit in Seattle.

02:29.941 --> 02:33.402
A guy named Isaac.
Supposedly, he'd take us all in.

02:33.403 --> 02:35.280
[Abby]
Not until we find Joel.

02:39.868 --> 02:43.078
We're finding him.
Yes, we are.

02:43.079 --> 02:44.581
Yes, we are.

02:47.333 --> 02:51.170
Alright, let's talk about how.
Because here's what we got.

02:51.171 --> 02:53.589
He's a smuggler.
His name's Joel or Joe.

02:53.590 --> 02:55.090
There's some confusion
about that--

02:55.091 --> 02:56.967
Fifties, graying, beard,
six foot tall,

02:56.968 --> 02:58.677
scar on his right temple.

02:58.678 --> 03:00.470
[chuckling] Oh, yeah.
They say he's handsome.

03:00.471 --> 03:01.597
I forgot.

03:01.598 --> 03:02.764
With a three-day jump on us.

03:02.765 --> 03:04.141
We should have gone
right after him.

03:04.142 --> 03:06.185
He drove away, Abby.
In our only working vehicle.

03:06.186 --> 03:07.729
And we were trying
to save the wounded.

03:09.522 --> 03:12.483
But we didn't save anyone,
did we?

03:15.195 --> 03:17.321
- It's not fucking fair.
- No.

03:17.322 --> 03:19.948
None of this
is fucking fair.

03:19.949 --> 03:21.993
- [Owen] Abby.
- [Nora sighs]

03:25.622 --> 03:26.664
Maybe...

03:27.999 --> 03:30.376
maybe the Seattle crew
has resources.

03:33.004 --> 03:34.756
They could help us
get some sort of lead.

03:37.759 --> 03:40.677
[sighs]
You'll help me find him.

03:40.678 --> 03:44.015
Yes.
We'll help you find him.

03:47.143 --> 03:48.937
Then, we'll help you kill him.

03:50.396 --> 03:51.397
[exhales deeply]

03:59.364 --> 04:02.242
[♪ solemn music playing]

04:09.582 --> 04:10.583
[sighs]

04:29.602 --> 04:30.852
[exhales sharply]

04:30.853 --> 04:32.897
[♪ music fades out]

04:37.944 --> 04:39.028
Slowly.

04:40.071 --> 04:41.072
[Owen] What?

04:44.993 --> 04:46.369
When we kill him...

04:50.123 --> 04:51.749
we kill him slowly.

05:00.466 --> 05:03.011
[♪ pensive theme music playing]

05:57.732 --> 05:59.442
[♪ theme concludes]

06:04.906 --> 06:08.200
[Caleb and Ellie grunting]

06:08.201 --> 06:09.327
[thuds]

06:10.953 --> 06:12.246
[Ellie coughs]

06:13.456 --> 06:14.998
- [Caleb] Get up.
- [panting]

06:14.999 --> 06:17.043
[♪ tense music playing]

06:18.795 --> 06:20.922
[Ellie grunting]

06:22.298 --> 06:23.841
[both grunting]

06:25.301 --> 06:27.552
- [Ellie exclaiming]
- Come on, let's go.

06:27.553 --> 06:29.347
[grunting and shouting
continues]

06:40.691 --> 06:42.193
[grunting continues]

06:43.986 --> 06:46.155
- [Ellie thuds]
- [both panting]

06:48.574 --> 06:50.618
[choking, grunting]

06:54.288 --> 06:55.289
[Ellie yelling]

06:56.332 --> 06:57.499
[Caleb yells]

06:57.500 --> 06:59.377
[both grunting]

07:01.045 --> 07:02.171
[banging]

07:03.089 --> 07:05.382
[Jesse]
Okay. Okay.

07:05.383 --> 07:07.342
- [banging]
- [Jesse] Ellie!

07:07.343 --> 07:10.805
[both panting]

07:13.599 --> 07:15.684
Boom, motherfucker.

07:15.685 --> 07:18.061
First of all,
"okay" means stop.

07:18.062 --> 07:19.855
Sorry, I was in the moment.

07:19.856 --> 07:21.773
Second, you can't
"Boom, motherfucker" people

07:21.774 --> 07:23.233
who land the first hit on you.

07:23.234 --> 07:24.693
Square in the face,
by the way.

07:24.694 --> 07:27.446
Well, I can obviously take
a punch, so who cares?

07:27.447 --> 07:29.698
- Fuckin' hard, by the way.
- I pulled it.

07:29.699 --> 07:31.908
- You-- you pulled it?
- Uh, yeah, he pulled it.

07:31.909 --> 07:33.618
- Why?
- 'Cause I told him to.

07:33.619 --> 07:36.204
- Why?
- Otherwise, he would
have knocked you out.

07:36.205 --> 07:38.666
And I don't want to have
to explain that to Joel.

07:41.752 --> 07:44.505
- Don't do that again.
- Okay.

07:47.925 --> 07:50.887
I should've closed in
faster on that one,
but the rest was good.

07:52.054 --> 07:53.347
The rest was good.

07:56.142 --> 07:58.560
You, uh, are you going
to the thing tonight?

07:58.561 --> 08:02.105
Don't we have to?
'Cause community and shit?

08:02.106 --> 08:04.149
[chuckles] Oh, you're part
of the community now?

08:04.150 --> 08:05.735
[Caleb laughing]

08:07.403 --> 08:08.737
Seriously, though, if you are,

08:08.738 --> 08:10.238
we could use
an extra pair of hands

08:10.239 --> 08:11.824
breaking down firewood
for the cookout.

08:13.201 --> 08:14.784
[water splashing]

08:14.785 --> 08:16.120
Don't pull punches.

08:22.293 --> 08:23.919
[horses whinnying]

08:23.920 --> 08:27.048
[♪ light music playing]

08:28.591 --> 08:30.760
[people chattering]

08:36.474 --> 08:38.142
[birds chirping]

08:45.066 --> 08:46.942
- [people chattering]
- [hammers clanking]

08:46.943 --> 08:48.319
[table saw whirring]

08:54.909 --> 08:56.869
[pieces clinking]

09:01.040 --> 09:03.292
[Dina]
Oh. Well, that's fucked.

09:05.336 --> 09:07.421
[distant hammering,
whirring continue]

09:22.812 --> 09:23.853
[door opens]

09:23.854 --> 09:24.980
[blowing]

09:24.981 --> 09:26.065
[door shuts]

09:26.816 --> 09:28.066
[footsteps approaching]

09:28.067 --> 09:30.026
[Dina] Hey.

09:30.027 --> 09:31.319
Hey, kiddo.

09:31.320 --> 09:32.363
[Dina sighs]

09:33.322 --> 09:34.698
Somethin' go wrong out there?

09:34.699 --> 09:37.033
Well, uh, the main lines
are clay,

09:37.034 --> 09:38.910
all cracked to shit
and full of roots.

09:38.911 --> 09:40.328
We're not sure what
we're supposed to do,

09:40.329 --> 09:42.831
and our foreman
isn't foreman-ing.

09:42.832 --> 09:43.833
Oh.

09:45.084 --> 09:47.003
Yeah, sorry.
I'll be out there in a minute.

09:49.046 --> 09:51.715
- Whatcha doin'?
- Fixing these breakers.

09:51.716 --> 09:53.174
They were gonna
chuck the whole panel,

09:53.175 --> 09:54.552
but all they need
is new springs.

09:57.096 --> 09:59.014
[chair scraping]

09:59.015 --> 10:00.057
Teach me?

10:03.811 --> 10:04.812
Okay.

10:06.731 --> 10:08.024
Uh, well...

10:09.609 --> 10:12.360
First thing first,
before you mess with circuits,

10:12.361 --> 10:13.737
you gotta check
if the wires are live.

10:13.738 --> 10:15.363
So, how do you do that?

10:15.364 --> 10:17.282
I...

10:17.283 --> 10:18.576
lick them?

10:21.621 --> 10:23.413
Voltage tester.

10:23.414 --> 10:25.540
[tapping]

10:25.541 --> 10:29.544
Now, this right here
is the part that matters.

10:29.545 --> 10:31.129
Bimetallic strip.

10:31.130 --> 10:34.049
Too much current runs through,
heats up the strip,

10:34.050 --> 10:37.594
it bends, releases the lever?
Circuit breaks.

10:37.595 --> 10:39.095
Otherwise, the wires
get hotter and hotter,

10:39.096 --> 10:41.264
lights the inside
of your walls on fire.

10:41.265 --> 10:43.308
There goes your house.

10:43.309 --> 10:45.311
- Can I ask a question?
- Shoot.

10:46.520 --> 10:48.856
Why is she angry at you?

10:52.443 --> 10:55.863
- She said she was angry?
- No, but...

11:01.160 --> 11:03.078
You're her best friend,
reckon she would have told you.

11:03.079 --> 11:05.122
[sighs] Nope.

11:08.000 --> 11:10.294
[♪ gentle music playing]

11:11.921 --> 11:14.172
Well, I figure it's normal.

11:14.173 --> 11:18.510
Her bein' 19 and me
bein' her... what I am.

11:18.511 --> 11:20.345
No one likes their parents
at that age.

11:20.346 --> 11:22.097
I never got there
with my own kid,

11:22.098 --> 11:24.725
so we're both
just figuring it out
for the first time, is all.

11:26.519 --> 11:27.728
We'll get through it.

11:28.813 --> 11:30.731
Yeah, that makes sense.

11:31.774 --> 11:34.360
- So, the springs hold
the levers back--
- The thing is, I try.

11:36.404 --> 11:38.613
I know I'm a hard-ass
and maybe overprotective,

11:38.614 --> 11:39.865
and she's...

11:41.200 --> 11:43.369
her, but...

11:45.830 --> 11:48.082
I mean, what did I do?

11:49.834 --> 11:51.043
I don't know.

11:53.921 --> 11:55.214
Yeah, well...

11:57.800 --> 11:59.467
I can't hold myself
responsible

11:59.468 --> 12:01.387
for another person's
emotional state.

12:04.306 --> 12:06.516
Are you in fucking therapy?

12:06.517 --> 12:09.185
[chuckles] Holy shit,
you're seeing Gail?

12:09.186 --> 12:11.147
I'm not in therapy.
Jesus, go...

12:12.314 --> 12:14.232
go fix the main line.

12:14.233 --> 12:15.900
Saw out the cracked parts,

12:15.901 --> 12:18.153
pull the roots
and we'll fill in the gaps
with some ABS.

12:18.154 --> 12:19.529
- Go on.
- [sighs]

12:19.530 --> 12:21.574
[sucks teeth]

12:24.118 --> 12:25.578
It'll be okay.

12:31.917 --> 12:33.002
Dina.

12:37.757 --> 12:39.759
Don't tell anyone
I'm in therapy.

12:48.350 --> 12:50.936
[door opens, closes]

12:53.606 --> 12:55.608
[wind blowing]

12:56.108 --> 12:58.110
[faint clicking]

13:00.404 --> 13:02.071
[gunshot blasts]

13:02.072 --> 13:03.239
[Ellie laughs]

13:03.240 --> 13:05.116
[Tommy laughing]
Oh, shit.

13:05.117 --> 13:07.035
This scope is sick.

13:07.036 --> 13:09.871
[chuckles] It ain't the scope,
it's the shooter.

13:09.872 --> 13:12.373
- You're gettin' good.
- Who's next?

13:12.374 --> 13:13.667
Let's see.

13:14.668 --> 13:16.878
Ah, okay.
There's a cluster of 'em

13:16.879 --> 13:18.546
up by the road.

13:18.547 --> 13:21.716
- One's broken away, you see him?
- See him.

13:21.717 --> 13:24.302
- Alright, you wanna take
your time with this one.
- [sniffles]

13:24.303 --> 13:25.846
It's further away, so more drop.

13:26.764 --> 13:28.641
He's going uphill,
so you gotta compensate.

13:30.351 --> 13:31.976
Head shot?

13:31.977 --> 13:34.480
- Always.
- [breathes deeply]

13:37.107 --> 13:39.150
[groaning]

13:39.151 --> 13:40.735
[raspy breaths]

13:40.736 --> 13:42.737
- [gunshot]
- [yelps, screeches]

13:42.738 --> 13:45.032
- Ah, fuck.
- Nah.

13:46.033 --> 13:47.992
It's alright,
you got him anyway.

13:47.993 --> 13:51.079
I guess.
A lot of them out there.

13:51.080 --> 13:52.413
Yeah, I noticed.

13:52.414 --> 13:54.124
Probably followin' down
Route 89.

13:55.918 --> 13:58.420
- Maybe comin' outta Alpine.
- Mm.

13:59.380 --> 14:02.090
We should head back.
I wanna get a patrol out there.

14:02.091 --> 14:04.343
Cool, I'll do that run.

14:05.302 --> 14:09.097
Actually, uh, I'm takin' you
off patrols for a bit.

14:09.098 --> 14:10.431
Puttin' you on gate watch.

14:10.432 --> 14:12.226
Gate watch?
What? Why?

14:13.435 --> 14:15.270
[groaning] Oh.
'Cause it's an important job.

14:15.271 --> 14:18.314
It's standing
on a fucking fence.

14:18.315 --> 14:19.859
He's concerned about you.

14:20.860 --> 14:22.944
Unfucking real.

14:22.945 --> 14:25.613
Well, you know, last run,
you were a bit reckless.

14:25.614 --> 14:27.949
It was two runners
and a Clicker
who barely had teeth.

14:27.950 --> 14:29.826
I handled it.
Isn't that the job?

14:29.827 --> 14:31.703
You wandered off
on your own, Ellie.

14:31.704 --> 14:33.830
- We have rules for reasons.
- Oh, please, Dina does this shit

14:33.831 --> 14:35.957
all the time,
no one's putting her
on the fucking fence.

14:35.958 --> 14:37.959
Tommy, I'm an adult.

14:37.960 --> 14:39.836
He can't tell me
what I can and can't do.

14:39.837 --> 14:42.089
- Yeah, well, he can tell me.
- [sighs]

14:43.215 --> 14:45.800
Look, I've been dealin'
with him my whole life.

14:45.801 --> 14:48.303
Sometimes,
easier to just go along.

14:48.304 --> 14:50.638
I don't care if it's easier.
It's not fair.

14:50.639 --> 14:52.056
And by the way,
you know I'm the one

14:52.057 --> 14:54.017
we should be least worried about
when it comes to infected.

14:54.018 --> 14:55.518
Hey, no.

14:55.519 --> 14:57.061
You swore.
We don't talk about that.

14:57.062 --> 14:58.980
I got bit on my arm.

14:58.981 --> 15:01.734
Ellie, we don't talk
about that.

15:03.193 --> 15:05.028
- I got bit, everybody!
- Hey!

15:05.029 --> 15:07.238
- I got bit!
- Hey! Hey, hey!

15:07.239 --> 15:08.823
I'm immune!

15:08.824 --> 15:10.241
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Hey!

15:10.242 --> 15:11.576
- Whoo!
- Jesus.

15:11.577 --> 15:13.454
- Goddammit.
- [Ellie panting]

15:14.538 --> 15:18.207
I swear, you and my brother?
Same goddamn fuckin' person.

15:18.208 --> 15:19.751
Well, if we're the same person,

15:19.752 --> 15:21.253
you know
you're not winning this.

15:24.423 --> 15:25.841
Put me on the patrol.

15:27.927 --> 15:28.928
[sighs]

15:30.554 --> 15:32.180
Alpine run leaves at 1300.

15:32.181 --> 15:34.016
[♪ light guitar music playing]

15:37.353 --> 15:39.854
Now, you follow the rules.

15:39.855 --> 15:41.731
You obey your captain.

15:41.732 --> 15:43.441
- [sighs]
- No questions, no exceptions.

15:43.442 --> 15:46.361
Well, that depends.
Who's the captain?

15:46.362 --> 15:49.614
- Ellie.
- Okay, fine. Whatever.

15:49.615 --> 15:51.158
I'll do it by the book.

15:54.995 --> 15:58.206
♪

15:58.207 --> 16:00.250
[rider]
Easy girl. Come on.

16:05.255 --> 16:07.758
- Open it up!
- [metal clanking]

16:10.594 --> 16:13.597
[people chattering]

16:19.019 --> 16:21.562
[Joel]
These three will be done
by next day or so.

16:21.563 --> 16:23.439
- [imitates airplane]
- Then another day
to hook up sewage.

16:23.440 --> 16:25.149
Now, y'all wanted the library

16:25.150 --> 16:26.943
and the school
restored by spring.

16:26.944 --> 16:28.569
But they both need new roofs.

16:28.570 --> 16:31.155
With the manpower that we have,
I-- I don't see any of this

16:31.156 --> 16:32.658
gettin' done until summer.

16:33.826 --> 16:36.411
This window isn't keepin'
the cold out anymore.

16:36.412 --> 16:40.164
Yeah, yeah. Caulk.
It's high up on my list.

16:40.165 --> 16:43.001
Uh, we've been using a ton of it
to restore the new, uh--

16:43.002 --> 16:45.421
- We need to build faster.
- Faster?

16:46.880 --> 16:48.423
Sure. How much faster?

16:48.424 --> 16:50.758
See, we got this, uh, dial,

16:50.759 --> 16:52.760
uh, called
the Constructo meter.

16:52.761 --> 16:54.679
- Joel.
- The more you turn it,
the faster we go.

16:54.680 --> 16:56.639
We're running out of space
to put these people.

16:56.640 --> 16:59.434
Yeah, I noticed.
Maybe your, uh, council

16:59.435 --> 17:00.977
would stop lettin'
so many of 'em in.

17:00.978 --> 17:02.603
[Maria] It's our council.

17:02.604 --> 17:04.605
And those people are fleeing
collapsed settlements.

17:04.606 --> 17:06.691
They're fleeing infected.
We're supposed to
leave them out there?

17:06.692 --> 17:09.945
If our lifeboat is swamped,
yeah, we leave 'em out there.

17:16.452 --> 17:20.663
[sighs] If I could,
I'd let 'em all in.

17:20.664 --> 17:22.957
And I'm workin'
every damn day and night

17:22.958 --> 17:24.959
to make more space,
you know that.

17:24.960 --> 17:26.627
But you got to look
after your own first,

17:26.628 --> 17:28.046
or you're no good to anyone.

17:28.047 --> 17:30.339
[footsteps approaching]

17:30.340 --> 17:32.133
- Uncle Joel.
- Hey, buddy.

17:32.134 --> 17:34.969
- What are those?
- Come here.

17:34.970 --> 17:36.846
[grunting]

17:36.847 --> 17:38.222
Okay, we're lookin' at maps.

17:38.223 --> 17:39.515
See?

17:39.516 --> 17:41.809
- This is where we live.
- [Benji] Mm-hmm.

17:41.810 --> 17:43.811
- And what's that?
- [Benji] The fence.

17:43.812 --> 17:45.480
- And what's inside?
- [Benji] People!

17:45.481 --> 17:47.648
- And what's outside?
- Monsters.

17:47.649 --> 17:49.317
That's right.
And how do we keep 'em out?

17:49.318 --> 17:52.236
- We shoot them.
- [Joel] What do you mean, "we"?

17:52.237 --> 17:53.988
[whispering]
Are you shootin' monsters?

17:53.989 --> 17:55.823
- No.
- Are you shootin' monsters?

17:55.824 --> 17:57.075
- [chuckling] No.
- You are. You are.

17:57.076 --> 17:58.534
- Hey.
- You're shootin' monsters!

17:58.535 --> 17:59.660
- [laughing]
- Daddy!

17:59.661 --> 18:01.662
[Tommy]
There he is! Killer!

18:01.663 --> 18:03.832
Yeah. [chuckles]
I missed you, boy.

18:04.541 --> 18:05.875
Hey.

18:05.876 --> 18:08.002
Mm.
What y'all up to?

18:08.003 --> 18:09.670
Well, your wife wants me
to build faster.

18:09.671 --> 18:11.339
Did you tell her
about the big dial?

18:11.340 --> 18:13.549
[scoffs] Yeah, he told me.
Come here, baby.

18:13.550 --> 18:16.553
[chuckles] Ah!
You're getting so big.

18:20.599 --> 18:22.892
- You huntin', or...?
- [sighs] Infected.

18:22.893 --> 18:24.770
What? By yourself?

18:25.437 --> 18:26.605
Uh-huh, yeah.

18:30.067 --> 18:31.526
I gotta go.

18:31.527 --> 18:34.070
You keep gettin'
those monsters, Benji.

18:34.071 --> 18:37.198
- [Benji imitating gunshots]
- Oh! [grunts] Oh!

18:37.199 --> 18:39.075
Oh! Oh, you got me.

18:39.076 --> 18:41.119
- You got me.
- [Benji chuckles]

18:41.120 --> 18:42.329
[Maria] Joel.

18:43.872 --> 18:45.541
You were a refugee too.

18:53.465 --> 18:55.467
[♪ soft music playing]

18:58.428 --> 19:00.347
[fire crackling]

19:02.182 --> 19:03.891
[knocking]

19:03.892 --> 19:05.185
[Gail] It's open.

19:10.149 --> 19:11.567
I'll be right there.

19:24.496 --> 19:26.206
[dishes clinking in other room]

19:30.419 --> 19:32.421
[♪ soft music continues]

19:33.338 --> 19:36.007
[Gail] Do you want
anything to drink?

19:36.008 --> 19:37.425
What do you have?

19:37.426 --> 19:39.136
Whiskey.
Herbal tea.

19:40.470 --> 19:43.098
But the tea's mostly
thistles and dirt, so...

19:54.651 --> 19:56.652
[glasses clinking]

19:56.653 --> 19:57.988
What's the occasion?

19:58.947 --> 20:00.699
It's my birthday.

20:05.204 --> 20:07.414
Well, you wanna
start or what?

20:16.965 --> 20:19.008
Shake and stems.
What am I, in high school?

20:19.009 --> 20:21.135
[Joel]
It's winter, Gail.

20:21.136 --> 20:24.555
That never stopped Eugene.
January, February,

20:24.556 --> 20:26.892
the man would grow buds
the size of pinecones.

20:28.393 --> 20:29.603
Sticky as glue.

20:34.107 --> 20:35.317
Payment accepted.

20:40.656 --> 20:43.116
[timer clicking]

20:43.867 --> 20:45.993
Didn't know psychiatrists
were allowed to drink

20:45.994 --> 20:47.745
in these things.

20:47.746 --> 20:49.080
[Gail]
Psychotherapist.

20:49.081 --> 20:50.916
Psychiatrists
are the pill ones.

20:51.917 --> 20:54.252
And, no, we're not allowed
to drink in these things.

20:54.253 --> 20:56.712
But I woke up
this morning feeling sad.

20:56.713 --> 21:00.968
It's my first birthday
without my husband in 41 years.

21:10.936 --> 21:12.020
Tick, tick, tick.

21:17.734 --> 21:20.695
Well, I tried what you said.
I backed off.

21:20.696 --> 21:22.238
I stopped
puttin' pressure on her.

21:22.239 --> 21:24.407
Don't even make her
sit down with me
for dinner anymore.

21:24.408 --> 21:26.784
And what do I get for it?
Nothin'.

21:26.785 --> 21:28.869
She comes home, shuts herself
in the damn garage,

21:28.870 --> 21:31.289
which I should never have
allowed her to move into.

21:31.290 --> 21:33.834
And that's it.
Not so much as a hello.

21:35.168 --> 21:37.211
I see her around town.
Gives me a nod

21:37.212 --> 21:39.213
like I'm a stranger
or some asshole.

21:39.214 --> 21:41.549
Even Dina asked me today,
"What's wrong with her?"

21:41.550 --> 21:43.050
I mean, everyone can tell.

21:43.051 --> 21:44.761
Now, that one.

21:46.596 --> 21:48.390
That one treats me
like a human being.

21:49.474 --> 21:51.809
She talks to me,
says "Hello,"

21:51.810 --> 21:53.769
gives me a smile,
looks up to me,

21:53.770 --> 21:56.063
makes me feel like
I'm a good guy, which I am.

21:56.064 --> 21:57.606
See, Dina understands me.

21:57.607 --> 21:59.609
Like she's my kid or somethin'.

22:02.321 --> 22:03.405
But she's not.

22:04.948 --> 22:06.533
Mm, neither is Ellie.

22:08.785 --> 22:09.870
Tell you what.

22:11.121 --> 22:12.998
Let's try something different.

22:15.959 --> 22:18.252
- Like what?
- [groans] Like not pretending

22:18.253 --> 22:20.839
you have the most boring
problem in the world.

22:21.590 --> 22:23.132
[mocking]
"Oh, a 19-year-old daughter.

22:23.133 --> 22:26.427
"She's acting toward me like
every 19-year-old daughter

22:26.428 --> 22:29.263
has ever acted
toward their dad, ever."

22:29.264 --> 22:31.432
What is this,
our fifth session?

22:31.433 --> 22:35.186
Are you just gonna keep
grouching on like this
every time?

22:35.187 --> 22:37.731
Aren't you supposed to be
validating me or somethin'?

22:38.732 --> 22:41.234
Oh, yeah, actually, I am.

22:42.235 --> 22:44.487
Uh, but I'm not
gonna do it anymore

22:44.488 --> 22:45.863
because you're lying to me,

22:45.864 --> 22:47.656
- and it's exhausting.
- [scoffs]

22:47.657 --> 22:50.493
Yes, you are, Joel.
Yes, you are.

22:50.494 --> 22:52.495
I've done this
long enough to know

22:52.496 --> 22:54.121
when somebody is leaving
something out.

22:54.122 --> 22:56.958
And you are definitely
leaving something out.

22:57.959 --> 22:59.835
And you want me
to validate that?

22:59.836 --> 23:01.337
No.

23:01.338 --> 23:03.173
In fact, fuck, no.

23:08.178 --> 23:10.638
- That's not your
first one of the day.
- Oh, no, it isn't.

23:10.639 --> 23:12.139
And before,
when I said I was sad,

23:12.140 --> 23:13.224
that wasn't true either.

23:13.225 --> 23:15.142
I'll just come back
another day.

23:15.143 --> 23:16.728
Should I say it out loud?

23:19.856 --> 23:21.108
Yeah, I should.

23:24.069 --> 23:26.153
You can't heal something
unless you're brave enough

23:26.154 --> 23:27.656
to say it out loud.

23:32.119 --> 23:35.204
[whispering] I'm scared though.
[chuckles softly]

23:35.205 --> 23:36.957
I'm scared to say it.

23:37.999 --> 23:39.751
Which is why I have to.

23:43.839 --> 23:46.674
You shot and killed
my husband.

23:46.675 --> 23:48.509
[sighs]

23:48.510 --> 23:51.178
You killed Eugene.

23:51.179 --> 23:53.264
And I resent you for it.

23:53.265 --> 23:56.267
No.
Maybe a little more than that.

23:56.268 --> 24:00.856
I hate you for it.
I hate you for it.

24:01.773 --> 24:04.191
And, yes, I know
you had no choice.

24:04.192 --> 24:06.987
I know that.
I know I should forgive you.

24:08.280 --> 24:10.323
Well, I've tried, and I can't...

24:11.324 --> 24:14.119
because of how you did it.

24:15.912 --> 24:20.625
And looking at your face
sitting in our home...

24:22.252 --> 24:25.005
makes me so fucking angry.

24:34.014 --> 24:36.891
There it is.
I've said it.

24:36.892 --> 24:39.059
I'm ashamed.

24:39.060 --> 24:42.314
But it's in the air
and I can't take it back.

24:46.193 --> 24:48.068
And now,
maybe there's a chance

24:48.069 --> 24:49.988
I can make things
right with you.

24:53.783 --> 24:54.910
Your turn.

24:56.703 --> 24:59.581
Say the thing
you're afraid to say.

25:02.751 --> 25:04.919
I can help you.

25:04.920 --> 25:06.921
Say it out loud,
no matter what it is.

25:06.922 --> 25:11.009
No matter how bad.
I promise, I will help.

25:17.098 --> 25:18.892
Did you do something to her?

25:22.062 --> 25:24.064
[breathing shakily]

25:26.191 --> 25:27.942
Did you hurt her?

25:27.943 --> 25:29.944
[whispering]
No. No.

25:29.945 --> 25:31.196
Then, what?

25:32.322 --> 25:34.114
What did you do?

25:34.115 --> 25:36.243
[♪ soft, solemn music playing]

25:56.012 --> 25:57.639
I saved her.

26:01.560 --> 26:04.563
[door opens, closes]

26:10.235 --> 26:12.237
[bird cawing]

26:13.071 --> 26:14.823
[gate creaking]

26:15.991 --> 26:17.993
[melted snow dripping]

26:20.954 --> 26:22.956
- [birds cawing]
- [chair creaking]

26:24.833 --> 26:27.335
[♪ muffled rock music playing]

26:30.255 --> 26:32.257
[light scraping]

26:34.342 --> 26:38.178
[♪ "Love Buzz" by Nirvana
playing over speakers]

26:38.179 --> 26:40.223
[soft metallic clinking]

26:41.433 --> 26:44.059
[scrubbing]

26:44.060 --> 26:46.688
♪ Please don't deceive me
when I hurt you ♪

26:47.147 --> 26:49.357
♪ Just ain't the way it seems ♪

26:50.358 --> 26:54.236
♪ Can you feel my love buzz? ♪

26:54.237 --> 26:57.531
♪ Can you feel
my love buzz? ♪

26:57.532 --> 27:00.409
- ♪ Can you feel my love buzz? ♪
- [gun clicks, thuds]

27:00.410 --> 27:02.620
[heavy knocks at door]

27:02.621 --> 27:05.122
♪ Can you feel my love buzz? ♪

27:05.123 --> 27:07.041
- [♪ music stops]
- Coming.

27:07.042 --> 27:08.585
[sighs]

27:10.253 --> 27:11.795
Hi.

27:11.796 --> 27:13.047
Came to pick you up.

27:13.048 --> 27:14.883
- Oh, you're on this run?
- Uh-huh.

27:16.509 --> 27:18.052
Uh, give me a second.

27:18.053 --> 27:20.971
Take as much time as you need.
Two minutes.

27:20.972 --> 27:22.598
Uh...

27:22.599 --> 27:25.559
I, uh, heard you were getting
stuck on the fence today.

27:25.560 --> 27:27.854
- Mm.
- How'd you get out of that?

27:28.772 --> 27:31.024
- Tommy.
- [whispering] Tommy.

27:32.859 --> 27:34.652
[normal]
Ooh, where'd you get
the holster?

27:34.653 --> 27:38.113
Dominique.
Traded some old boots for it.

27:38.114 --> 27:39.449
- [clears throat]
- Huh.

27:41.493 --> 27:42.911
Should've kept
the boots.

27:44.371 --> 27:45.954
- [sighs]
- Here, let me help.

27:45.955 --> 27:47.623
- I can do it.
- Oh, it's okay.

27:47.624 --> 27:49.167
I got it.
There we go.

27:50.168 --> 27:51.919
Just like that.
Hold on.

27:51.920 --> 27:54.463
Let me get this part here.

27:54.464 --> 27:57.884
Yep. 'Cause now...
There we go.

27:58.760 --> 28:00.260
[sighs]

28:00.261 --> 28:02.305
- Better?
- Yeah, better.

28:02.931 --> 28:05.182
Look at you
with all that hardware.

28:05.183 --> 28:06.726
You're like Curtis and Viper.

28:08.019 --> 28:09.603
You know th-those movies
Joel likes?

28:09.604 --> 28:11.146
Yeah, I know.

28:11.147 --> 28:12.606
I was actually gonna
maybe watch them

28:12.607 --> 28:14.776
tomorrow night with him,
if you wanna join.

28:16.361 --> 28:18.112
Patrol?

28:18.113 --> 28:20.323
Yeah.
Yeah, patrol.

28:23.076 --> 28:24.868
- Why, thank you.
- You're welcome.

28:24.869 --> 28:25.954
Yeah.

28:27.122 --> 28:28.748
[horse snorts]

28:34.963 --> 28:36.505
Hey, Shimmer.

28:36.506 --> 28:38.340
- [whispering] Hi, girl.
- [Shimmer grunts]

28:38.341 --> 28:39.384
[Dina] Ellie.

28:46.599 --> 28:47.808
[sighs]

28:47.809 --> 28:49.852
[people chattering]

28:49.853 --> 28:51.146
[horse whinnies]

28:51.896 --> 28:53.440
[Jesse]
Oh, there we go.

28:55.316 --> 28:59.528
Okay, we're five minutes behind
because of one or two of you,

28:59.529 --> 29:01.572
so I'll make it short.

29:01.573 --> 29:03.407
You're doing the Alpine run.

29:03.408 --> 29:06.410
I know a couple of you
are new to this trail,
so listen up.

29:06.411 --> 29:09.164
You're taking Route 191
down to Hoback.

29:10.915 --> 29:12.082
- Yes, Dina.
- Hi.

29:12.083 --> 29:13.584
Um, should we stick
to the road,

29:13.585 --> 29:15.335
scan the countryside,
hit our checkpoints,

29:15.336 --> 29:17.838
and sign the log books?

29:17.839 --> 29:21.008
[chuckles] You know what?
That sounds great.

29:21.009 --> 29:23.844
But while you're doing all that,
we've got reports of strays.

29:23.845 --> 29:25.847
So, be careful
when you get into the town.

29:26.848 --> 29:29.850
Now, I see Ellie over here
looking like Curtis and Viper.

29:29.851 --> 29:31.935
- The fuck?
- [Jesse] So, let me remind you,

29:31.936 --> 29:34.396
this is just a recon patrol.

29:34.397 --> 29:36.899
If you see one or two runners,
that's fine, clear 'em out.

29:36.900 --> 29:39.234
Anything more,
anything worse,

29:39.235 --> 29:41.695
you come on back
and we send out a squad.
Understood?

29:41.696 --> 29:44.740
You know you're only, like,
four years older than us, right?

29:44.741 --> 29:46.659
Just say, "Understood."

29:49.621 --> 29:51.705
- Understood.
- Thank you.

29:51.706 --> 29:55.793
Your patrol leader is Kat,
so you will follow her orders.

29:55.794 --> 29:57.252
[metal clanking]

29:57.253 --> 29:59.755
When you're back, today's
all-clear sign is yellow.

29:59.756 --> 30:02.050
Yellow, good.
Green, bad.

30:04.677 --> 30:08.014
Jokes aside, can you take
things a little more seriously?

30:10.892 --> 30:12.393
The others look up to you two.

30:14.103 --> 30:15.814
For some fuckin' reason.

30:17.232 --> 30:20.150
Okay, Alpine run,
moving out!

30:20.151 --> 30:22.570
[gate guard] Alpine run!
Moving out, let's go!

30:26.032 --> 30:28.034
- [people chattering]
- [horses snorting]

30:31.996 --> 30:34.374
[♪ curious music playing]

30:35.583 --> 30:37.585
[gate rattling]

30:41.130 --> 30:42.257
[doors thud]

30:51.558 --> 30:53.560
[horses grunting softly]

31:10.869 --> 31:12.870
So, you going tonight?

31:12.871 --> 31:14.414
Yes, I'm going.

31:15.415 --> 31:16.583
Taking anyone?

31:19.294 --> 31:22.212
- No.
- Why not?

31:22.213 --> 31:24.464
- Kat's available.
- Why would I ask Kat?

31:24.465 --> 31:28.135
Because she's the other one.

31:28.136 --> 31:30.304
- Oh, my God.
- What?

31:30.305 --> 31:32.681
You used to with her.

31:32.682 --> 31:34.474
And she definitely
left her mark.

31:34.475 --> 31:36.852
Right, yes, thank you.

31:36.853 --> 31:37.937
But no.

31:40.732 --> 31:44.694
Ohh.
You're into someone else.

31:48.489 --> 31:50.490
Tell you what.
You can go with me.

31:50.491 --> 31:52.659
We can get baked.
We can dance

31:52.660 --> 31:54.870
to the smooth tunes of--
what are they called?

31:54.871 --> 31:57.748
Britney and the Jug Boys.
It'll be fun!

31:57.749 --> 31:59.249
We'll count down
to the New Year together.

31:59.250 --> 32:01.251
BFFs, 2029.

32:01.252 --> 32:03.378
- Aren't you and Jesse...?
- No.

32:03.379 --> 32:04.505
Broke up.

32:05.673 --> 32:06.799
Yes, again.

32:07.634 --> 32:08.718
For now.

32:10.219 --> 32:11.596
What is it with you two?

32:14.140 --> 32:15.433
I don't know.

32:17.018 --> 32:18.227
[Kat] Whoa!

32:20.980 --> 32:22.231
[Ellie clicks tongue]

32:26.527 --> 32:28.780
[♪ tense, curious music playing]

32:33.409 --> 32:35.619
[Dina pants]

32:35.620 --> 32:37.704
- Let's go.
- [chuckles]

32:37.705 --> 32:39.873
- Okay. We're on.
- [Kat] Wait.

32:39.874 --> 32:42.709
- [Dina clicks tongue]
- We should go back
and report it.

32:42.710 --> 32:44.878
We're recon, Kat.
Let's fuckin' recon.

32:44.879 --> 32:46.005
Wait, guys!

32:48.049 --> 32:49.717
Hey, come on.
Guys!

32:55.431 --> 32:58.601
[♪ unsettling music playing]

33:14.659 --> 33:16.202
[Ellie whistling]

33:17.203 --> 33:18.620
[Dina] Ugh.

33:18.621 --> 33:21.666
How many infected does it take
to bring down a bear?

33:23.376 --> 33:26.336
- [Ellie] Check out the van.
- [Dina] Ah!

33:26.337 --> 33:28.171
So, they've been sheltering
in the market.

33:28.172 --> 33:30.841
[Ellie] Yeah, it looks like
at least one of them
made it back in.

33:30.842 --> 33:33.260
Maybe needed a nap
after chomping that poor thing.

33:33.261 --> 33:35.263
[Ellie] Yeah.

33:36.139 --> 33:37.848
Hey...

33:37.849 --> 33:39.350
what do you call
a grizzly's ribs?

33:40.560 --> 33:42.103
Bear-b-cue.

33:46.441 --> 33:47.691
Did you just make that up?

33:47.692 --> 33:49.443
- Yeah.
- Bear-b-cue?

33:49.444 --> 33:50.652
- Yeah.
- Seriously?

33:50.653 --> 33:53.196
[both laughing]

33:53.197 --> 33:55.366
- [Dina sighs]
- [Ellie chuckles]

33:57.577 --> 33:59.453
So, you think Hungry Boy
is still alive in there?

33:59.454 --> 34:01.121
Fuckin' hope so.

34:01.122 --> 34:02.749
- Good. Oh.
- [horse snorts]

34:03.916 --> 34:05.292
Hi. Oh, hi there.

34:05.293 --> 34:06.586
- Here comes fun.
- [Dina] Hi.

34:07.420 --> 34:08.713
[Kat] Oh, my God.

34:10.715 --> 34:12.425
- Happy?
- [Ellie] Mm.

34:14.635 --> 34:16.220
[grunting]

34:17.138 --> 34:18.472
Hey, can we go back now, please?

34:18.473 --> 34:21.308
Uh, yeah, we will.
Promise.

34:21.309 --> 34:25.312
We're just gonna listen quick,
see if any are in there,

34:25.313 --> 34:27.314
which is definitely recon.

34:27.315 --> 34:30.317
Hey, you know,
maybe there's a regular person
who's trapped and needs help.

34:30.318 --> 34:32.569
Yeah, what if there's
a family in there?

34:32.570 --> 34:35.655
What if there's a toddler?
Or a baby?

34:35.656 --> 34:37.575
There's no babies in there.

34:39.327 --> 34:40.994
- Hey, come on.
- [Ellie sighs]

34:40.995 --> 34:42.080
[Kat] Rules!

34:44.415 --> 34:45.874
Fine.

34:45.875 --> 34:48.168
If you hear anything,
you come right back.

34:48.169 --> 34:49.462
Okay.

34:51.631 --> 34:53.216
You just gonna
let 'em go in?

34:54.133 --> 34:55.676
I'll give 'em five minutes.

34:56.636 --> 34:57.887
[muffled screeching]

35:02.892 --> 35:04.769
Two on one.
[exhales sharply]

35:05.728 --> 35:07.313
[muffled clicking]

35:08.815 --> 35:10.233
[screeching]

35:11.776 --> 35:13.903
[high-pitched shrieking]

35:17.657 --> 35:20.034
Okay, so one on one.
We've done that before.

35:20.243 --> 35:21.869
[distant growling]

35:23.329 --> 35:24.872
[distant screeching]

35:25.248 --> 35:27.875
If you'd rather let
the men handle it.

35:28.417 --> 35:30.253
[growling continues]

35:37.552 --> 35:40.096
[distant screeching continues]

35:51.149 --> 35:52.733
[distant growling]

36:00.158 --> 36:02.160
[soft, distant clicking]

36:04.537 --> 36:05.663
[distant screeching]

36:12.044 --> 36:15.715
[screeching, clicking continue]

36:24.724 --> 36:26.726
[soft growling]

36:28.769 --> 36:30.897
[snarling, clicking]

36:33.399 --> 36:35.359
[loud screeching]

36:38.321 --> 36:40.323
[distant screeching]

36:52.793 --> 36:54.711
[whispering] Two.

36:54.712 --> 36:56.214
[mouthing]
The bottle.

36:59.050 --> 37:00.468
[distant clicking, snarling]

37:13.522 --> 37:15.942
[imitates choking]

37:31.499 --> 37:34.043
[♪ tense music playing]

37:39.799 --> 37:41.801
[distant snarling]

37:59.944 --> 38:02.655
[loud screeching]

38:07.952 --> 38:09.954
- [glass shatters]
- [loud shrieking]

38:11.497 --> 38:13.499
[snarling, clicking]

38:16.502 --> 38:18.211
[shrieking]

38:18.212 --> 38:20.881
- [♪ tense music continues]
- [Ellie breathing heavily]

38:21.590 --> 38:22.758
[floor boards creaking]

38:23.718 --> 38:25.720
[grunting and shouting]

38:30.516 --> 38:32.685
- [Ellie grunting]
- [clicker choking, gurgling]

38:36.147 --> 38:37.897
[sighs]

38:37.898 --> 38:39.275
Fuck yeah.

38:41.027 --> 38:43.486
Did you get bit?
Do I have to shoot you
in the face?

38:43.487 --> 38:45.322
- Not today.
- Okay.

38:45.323 --> 38:47.366
- Nice.
- [panting]

38:48.659 --> 38:50.118
[chuckling] Oh, my God,
before we leave,

38:50.119 --> 38:51.578
you gotta check out
the employee--

38:51.579 --> 38:52.954
[screaming]

38:52.955 --> 38:55.415
- [crashing]
- [Dina] Ellie!

38:55.416 --> 38:57.625
Ellie! Ellie!

38:57.626 --> 38:59.336
[coughing]

38:59.337 --> 39:01.088
Ellie, are you okay?

39:02.256 --> 39:04.132
[groaning]

39:04.133 --> 39:05.258
I'm good.

39:05.259 --> 39:07.345
- [Dina sighs]
- [Ellie coughs]

39:08.554 --> 39:12.307
No-- [coughing]
Nothing's broken,
I don't think.

39:12.308 --> 39:14.434
- [Dina] Oh, shit.
- [Ellie coughs]

39:14.435 --> 39:15.685
Are you alone?

39:15.686 --> 39:17.021
Uh...

39:18.189 --> 39:20.191
[wind whistling]

39:23.361 --> 39:24.987
I don't hear anything.

39:26.155 --> 39:27.947
I think we're good.

39:27.948 --> 39:29.950
[groaning]

39:31.911 --> 39:33.245
[sighs]

39:34.955 --> 39:35.956
[groans]

39:38.542 --> 39:42.380
[Dina] Alright,
uh, let's figure out
how to get you out.

39:46.425 --> 39:48.968
Uh, I don't see a way out.

39:48.969 --> 39:51.471
- A bunch of padlocked doors.
- Okay.

39:51.472 --> 39:53.348
It's too far for me
to drop down,

39:53.349 --> 39:56.142
so I can find
a stairway or something

39:56.143 --> 39:57.977
and figure out a path
back up here.

39:57.978 --> 39:59.979
- Just stay put.
- Yeah.

39:59.980 --> 40:01.190
Ellie?

40:02.233 --> 40:03.567
Stay put.

40:04.652 --> 40:06.612
- Yeah.
- Alright.

40:14.870 --> 40:16.872
[wind whistling]

40:57.913 --> 40:59.372
[scurrying]

40:59.373 --> 41:00.374
[distant groan]

41:05.129 --> 41:07.381
[♪ tense, unsettling
music playing]

41:11.510 --> 41:12.511
[soft rasping]

41:16.849 --> 41:18.851
[♪ music intensifies]

41:25.649 --> 41:26.984
[rifle cocking loudly]

41:28.194 --> 41:30.196
[♪ music fades]

41:31.489 --> 41:33.491
[wind whistling]

41:44.877 --> 41:46.879
[♪ tense music playing]

42:21.539 --> 42:23.541
- [panting]
- [glass crushing]

42:25.209 --> 42:27.211
[♪ tense music continues]

42:42.393 --> 42:43.727
[sighs]

42:48.482 --> 42:50.693
[distant gasping]

42:58.033 --> 43:00.119
[gurgling, gasping]

43:01.870 --> 43:04.414
[straining, grunting]

43:04.415 --> 43:06.041
Run at me, fucker!

43:11.130 --> 43:12.339
Run at me!

43:12.590 --> 43:14.507
- [yelps]
- [Ellie gasps]

43:14.508 --> 43:16.510
[panting]

43:17.052 --> 43:19.054
[♪ dramatic music playing]

43:35.863 --> 43:37.865
[breathing heavily]

43:54.298 --> 43:56.300
[softly grunts]

44:00.554 --> 44:02.556
[Ellie panting]

44:04.808 --> 44:06.810
[grunting]

44:08.812 --> 44:10.814
[wheezing]

44:15.402 --> 44:17.404
[softly grunting]

44:19.490 --> 44:20.574
[groans]

44:22.242 --> 44:23.618
- [shouting]
- [gunshot blasts]

44:23.619 --> 44:24.662
[debris clatters]

44:28.123 --> 44:30.083
[screaming]

44:30.084 --> 44:32.169
[grunting, shouting]

44:37.424 --> 44:39.510
[screaming]

44:43.305 --> 44:44.723
[screaming]

44:45.641 --> 44:47.308
- [grunting]
- [gunshot]

44:47.309 --> 44:48.352
[gunshot]

44:49.520 --> 44:52.189
[infected groaning]

44:54.566 --> 44:56.568
[breathing heavily]

45:01.198 --> 45:02.408
Fuck.

45:05.452 --> 45:07.830
[Dina]
Ellie, are you okay?!
Ellie, it's me!

45:08.497 --> 45:09.872
[panting] Over here!

45:09.873 --> 45:11.917
[running footsteps]

45:13.210 --> 45:15.963
[panting]
Oh, shit. You okay?

45:16.797 --> 45:17.965
Yeah.

45:18.382 --> 45:19.967
[Dina exhales sharply]

45:21.552 --> 45:23.636
- That was it?
- [Ellie groans]

45:23.637 --> 45:26.515
- Just her?
- Just her.

45:27.558 --> 45:29.560
[wind whistling]

45:31.520 --> 45:33.981
[Tommy]
So, you're saying it was,
what?

45:34.898 --> 45:36.232
Smart?

45:36.233 --> 45:38.151
I'm not saying
it could do math or anything,

45:38.152 --> 45:39.527
but it didn't run at me.

45:39.528 --> 45:43.197
It did what we do--
took cover, planned, waited,

45:43.198 --> 45:45.366
lured me in.

45:45.367 --> 45:46.493
Stalking.

45:48.287 --> 45:50.163
- And you saw this?
- [Dina] Mm-hmm.

45:50.164 --> 45:52.249
It was exactly
like Ellie says.

45:53.625 --> 45:55.084
And how exactly does

45:55.085 --> 45:57.211
you two runnin' into
an uncleared building

45:57.212 --> 46:00.590
qualify as following the rules
and obeying your captain?

46:00.591 --> 46:02.717
Well, it wasn't like
this is our first time.

46:02.718 --> 46:04.761
We've killed
a lot of infected before.

46:04.762 --> 46:07.346
And you're telling me, what,
if it were you and Joel,
you wouldn't have gone in?

46:07.347 --> 46:09.599
- Well, that ain't the same.
- [Ellie] Why?

46:09.600 --> 46:11.185
- 'Cause it's different.
- How?

46:14.104 --> 46:16.689
Alright.
Apologize to Kat

46:16.690 --> 46:19.777
and log your report
with Jesse. Go.

46:27.618 --> 46:29.828
[door opens, closes]

46:30.537 --> 46:31.954
Do we believe them?

46:31.955 --> 46:33.956
Dina was lying.
She didn't see anything.

46:33.957 --> 46:35.708
But I believe Ellie.

46:35.709 --> 46:37.877
Maybe this smart one
was a one-off.

46:37.878 --> 46:39.879
Maybe.

46:39.880 --> 46:41.923
But what about the other six
that brought down the grizzly?

46:41.924 --> 46:44.801
Yeah, well, six ain't good,
but it's not exactly a horde.

46:44.802 --> 46:46.261
Not yet.

46:47.012 --> 46:49.972
I don't know, just lately,
I've had a feeling.

46:49.973 --> 46:51.433
A feeling?

46:54.102 --> 46:56.605
"Reality is nothing
but a collective hunch."

47:00.025 --> 47:01.860
- Lily Tomlin.
- [Maria chuckles softly]

47:03.737 --> 47:05.280
Four hours till New Year's.

47:06.323 --> 47:07.616
We adjourned?

47:08.742 --> 47:09.827
Adjourned.

47:11.995 --> 47:14.832
[council members
muttering indistinctly]

47:17.251 --> 47:18.335
[Ellie sighs]

47:18.710 --> 47:20.712
[♪ gentle music playing]

47:39.398 --> 47:40.607
[softly winces]

47:42.109 --> 47:43.318
[grunting]

48:00.752 --> 48:02.671
[exhales slowly]

48:04.256 --> 48:05.257
[knife clatters]

48:35.537 --> 48:36.747
[knocking]

48:39.166 --> 48:40.250
Come in.

48:44.296 --> 48:45.422
Ellie.

48:46.715 --> 48:47.716
[lights click]

48:48.592 --> 48:50.636
- Better?
- Nope.

48:52.554 --> 48:53.680
Okay.

48:56.558 --> 48:59.936
Just come to see
if you were going
to that thing tonight.

48:59.937 --> 49:01.396
Be good to show your face.

49:02.147 --> 49:04.398
I don't know.
Yeah, uh, maybe.

49:04.399 --> 49:05.651
I don't know.

49:11.865 --> 49:13.450
You been playin' much?

49:15.077 --> 49:16.286
Enough, yeah.

49:17.454 --> 49:18.830
[clears throat]

49:20.415 --> 49:22.250
[guitar string ringing]

49:30.384 --> 49:31.884
[Joel]
Strings are shot.

49:31.885 --> 49:33.386
- Well--
- I'll put some
new ones on for ya.

49:33.387 --> 49:34.720
Oh, you don't have
to do that, I--

49:34.721 --> 49:36.306
I can get it
back tomorrow.

49:40.185 --> 49:41.186
[door closes]

49:42.270 --> 49:45.482
[♪ "Little Sadie"
by Crooked Still playing]

49:48.151 --> 49:51.154
[people chattering, laughing]

49:54.992 --> 49:56.994
[children shouting]

49:57.452 --> 49:59.453
[dog barking]

49:59.454 --> 50:01.831
♪ I woke up in the morning
about half-past-nine ♪

50:01.832 --> 50:04.083
♪ The hacks and the buggies
standin' in line ♪

50:04.084 --> 50:06.252
♪ Gents and gamblers
standin' around ♪

50:06.253 --> 50:09.923
♪ Takin' Little Sadie
to her burying ground ♪

50:12.009 --> 50:14.301
♪ I began to think of
what a deed I'd done ♪

50:14.302 --> 50:15.428
[Dina] Whoo!

50:15.429 --> 50:17.471
[laughter, chatter continue]

50:17.472 --> 50:19.265
♪ Made a good run,
just a little too slow ♪

50:19.266 --> 50:21.434
♪ They overtook me
in Jericho ♪

50:21.435 --> 50:22.769
[laughing] Oh, sorry!

50:25.439 --> 50:26.981
♪

50:26.982 --> 50:28.691
[chuckles softly]

50:28.692 --> 50:31.277
♪ Standin' on the corner
a reading a bill ♪

50:31.278 --> 50:33.320
[Dina laughing]

50:33.321 --> 50:35.448
- Woo!
- [chatter continues]

50:35.449 --> 50:38.952
♪ Remember the night you
shot Sadie down? ♪

50:39.661 --> 50:43.206
♪ I said, "Oh yes sir,
but my name is Lee... ♪

50:44.041 --> 50:46.792
Oh, I hate these things.

50:46.793 --> 50:48.627
Tell me about it.

50:48.628 --> 50:51.131
Had to get half-drunk
just to show up.

50:52.841 --> 50:54.550
She's putting
on quite the show.

50:54.551 --> 50:56.552
- [chuckles softly]
- [guest] Happy New Year!

50:56.553 --> 50:58.471
[♪ plays flourishing finish]

50:58.472 --> 51:00.347
[laughing]

51:00.348 --> 51:02.392
[cheering and applause]

51:04.394 --> 51:07.481
You guys will be back
together in two weeks, tops.

51:08.982 --> 51:10.233
Not gonna happen.

51:13.070 --> 51:14.820
- Why?
- Ellie! Hey!

51:14.821 --> 51:16.322
What took you so long?

51:16.323 --> 51:18.741
[performer]
Okay, this next one
is a little slower.

51:18.742 --> 51:20.201
- It's one of our favorites.
- Come on!

51:20.202 --> 51:21.368
- But--
- Let's go!

51:21.369 --> 51:22.912
Hey, don't forget,
you got early patrol,

51:22.913 --> 51:25.332
- so get some rest.
- Sir, yes, sir.

51:27.667 --> 51:30.170
[♪ "Ecstasy"
by Crooked Still playing]

51:34.341 --> 51:36.343
[both giggling]

51:39.930 --> 51:42.933
Okay, I have a very serious
question for you.

51:44.267 --> 51:46.353
- How bad do I smell?
- [chuckles]

51:47.687 --> 51:50.356
[inhales deeply]

51:50.357 --> 51:54.360
Like a hot pile of garbage.

51:54.361 --> 51:57.363
Oh, okay.

51:57.364 --> 51:58.864
- [chuckles]
- Yeah.

51:58.865 --> 52:01.283
Oh! Oh!
[laughing]

52:01.284 --> 52:03.536
- Gross.
- [laughing]

52:03.537 --> 52:05.579
- You're so drunk.
- Uh-uh.

52:05.580 --> 52:08.457
I'm high.
Smoked a lot.

52:08.458 --> 52:09.750
Mm.

52:09.751 --> 52:13.546
♪ Oh, when shall
I see Jesus ♪

52:13.547 --> 52:19.553
♪ And reign
with him above ♪

52:24.099 --> 52:27.893
♪ And from
the flowing fountain ♪

52:27.894 --> 52:33.191
♪ Drink everlasting love ♪

52:38.905 --> 52:41.323
Every guy in this room
is staring at you right now.

52:41.324 --> 52:45.077
♪ Oh, had I wings
I would fly ♪

52:45.078 --> 52:46.495
♪ Fly away ♪

52:46.496 --> 52:49.833
Maybe they're staring
at you.

52:52.586 --> 52:54.004
They're not.

52:56.089 --> 52:58.007
Maybe...

52:58.008 --> 53:01.094
they're jealous of you.

53:03.597 --> 53:07.392
No reason to be.
I'm not a threat.

53:07.976 --> 53:11.938
♪ Whene'er you
meet with troubles... ♪

53:12.272 --> 53:13.440
[whispering]
Oh, Ellie.

53:16.276 --> 53:19.362
I think they should be
terrified of you.

53:22.324 --> 53:25.826
♪ Cast all your cares
on Jesus ♪

53:25.827 --> 53:30.999
♪ And don't forget to pray ♪

53:37.464 --> 53:43.261
♪ Ooh, had I wings
I would fly ♪

53:43.803 --> 53:44.845
♪ Fly away ♪

53:44.846 --> 53:45.931
[Seth] Hey.

53:48.391 --> 53:49.768
It's a family event.

53:51.811 --> 53:53.021
Sorry.

53:57.567 --> 53:58.817
Sorry!

53:58.818 --> 54:00.570
[people murmuring]

54:02.280 --> 54:04.323
- [scoffs]
- [Seth] You're in a church.

54:04.324 --> 54:06.075
- Dykes.
- The fuck did you just say?

54:06.076 --> 54:07.660
[Dina] Ellie, no. Ellie.

54:07.661 --> 54:08.827
- [grunting]
- [crowd gasping]

54:08.828 --> 54:10.079
[Joel]
Get the hell outta here.

54:10.080 --> 54:11.539
- [crowd murmuring]
- [guest] Jesus!

54:12.415 --> 54:15.209
- Seth, let's...
- [grunting]

54:15.210 --> 54:17.836
Let's take a walk.

54:17.837 --> 54:19.464
Come on. Let's go.

54:21.299 --> 54:22.759
Are you okay?

54:23.969 --> 54:26.263
What is wrong with you?

54:30.225 --> 54:33.686
I don't need
your fucking help.

54:33.687 --> 54:36.064
[♪ soft, solemn music playing]

54:36.231 --> 54:38.316
[crowd murmuring]

54:39.234 --> 54:40.485
Right.

54:57.502 --> 55:00.130
[door opens, shuts]

55:02.590 --> 55:03.800
[Ellie sighs]

55:05.510 --> 55:07.512
[people laughing]

55:08.388 --> 55:10.264
[people cheering]

55:10.265 --> 55:12.559
- [guest 1] There ya go!
- [cheering continues]

55:14.019 --> 55:15.227
[guest 2] Cheers!

55:15.228 --> 55:18.064
[guest 3]
Happy fucking New Year!
[laughing]

55:22.694 --> 55:24.696
[distant laughter,
cheering continue]

55:27.240 --> 55:29.826
[♪ guitar softly playing]

55:35.206 --> 55:36.541
[♪ stops playing guitar]

55:40.462 --> 55:42.464
[wind blowing]

56:06.446 --> 56:08.155
- Same thing.
- [laughing] I know.

56:08.156 --> 56:09.531
We started
at the party too, man.

56:09.532 --> 56:11.658
- I know.
- [laughing]

56:11.659 --> 56:13.619
Oh! Whoo!

56:13.620 --> 56:15.621
Oh, my God.

56:15.622 --> 56:17.624
[people chattering]

56:22.837 --> 56:24.839
[♪ tense, unsettling
music playing]

56:30.970 --> 56:33.306
[fungus crackling]

56:54.244 --> 56:56.538
[heavy breathing]

57:21.813 --> 57:23.815
[♪ music intensifies]
